WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.960
Hi, I’m Marie, and welcome to LearnKey’s
course on Databases.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.340
This course covers the material on the IT
Specialist Databases exam.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:15.210
If you ever wondered how to build and manage
databases properly, this course is for you.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.500
Building a database is not just a matter of
typing data into a spreadsheet.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.869
There is a lot of organization involved, and
Senior Instructor, Jason Manibog, is standing

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:26.339
by.

00:00:26.339 --> 00:00:31.599
This IT Specialist course on Databases is
a solid foundational course for building databases

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:34.750
and working with existing databases.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.500
Not only will this course help you prepare
to take and pass the Certiport IT Specialist

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.410
Database exam, but this course will also help
you gain employability prospects in the role

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.450
of a data specialist or even a junior database
administrator.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.980
In fact, that is the mentality I want you
to have for this course, that you are being

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:56.100
trained to become a junior database administrator
for a retail bicycle company.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.480
For this course, you will want to have access
to a SQL Server installation, whether you

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.600
download and install it or have access to
one in Azure.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.040
You will also want to get the sample AdventureWorks
database to follow along with the course videos

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.310
and projects.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.550
Links to the SQL Server download and the sample
database tend to change, so I would use a

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.070
search engine to find both.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:19.430
There are instructions for getting the database
loaded into SQL Server once you have installed

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:22.570
SQL Server and obtained the database.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:26.510
By the way, you will want the OLTP version
of the database as that will give you the

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:30.120
most opportunity to practice the skills you
will learn in this course.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.640
On to the course itself, there are five domains
in this course.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:41.930
They are: Database Design, Database Object
Management, Data Retrieval, Data Manipulation,

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:48.870
and Troubleshooting With the course, you get
the instructional videos, pre and post-assessments

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:53.870
for each domain, practice labs, and a project
workbook to reinforce what you learn in this

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.090
course.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.630
To work well with databases, one needs a solid
understanding of database design, which is

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:04.460
the first domain of this course, so let's
get right to the first topic, which is identifying

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:05.649
parts of a database.

